# Corporate — architecture rules

Corporate is a hosted, cloud-native multi-agent web app: a 2D office-floor UI where department agent teams work under a CEO orchestrator, visible through a "Command Center" dashboard.

```
/frontend    React + Vite + TS, Pixi.js office floor, xterm.js trace widget
/backend     Python 3.12, FastAPI, Google ADK
/departments Declarative per-department YAML config
/shared      Cross-language schema definitions
/infra       gcloud/firebase deployment scripts
/docs        ADRs, system_prompt.md, architecture diagram
```

## Backend: Python only, ADK only

- One language for the whole backend: Python. No department introduces a second language or agent framework.
- Pin `google-adk==2.7.1`. Requires Python 3.11+. Don't mix ADK 1.x and 2.x session/storage data.
- The only LLM in the shipped product is Gemini via Vertex AI. No other provider, no raw API key.
- Agents are `LlmAgent`/`SequentialAgent`/`ParallelAgent`/`LoopAgent`. Use workflow-agent composition only *within* one department's own pipeline — CEO-to-department delegation goes over Pub/Sub, never `sub_agents=`.
- Sessions are Firestore-backed (`FirestoreSessionService`), never `InMemorySessionService` — Cloud Run instances are ephemeral.

## State and messaging

- Firestore holds all durable state, namespaced `orgs/{orgId}/...`.
- Pub/Sub carries live inter-agent messages on one `agent-bus` topic, one push subscription per agent. Message schema: `{id, conversation, in_reply_to, from, to, act, subject, body, hops, requires_reply, needs_human, created_at}` where `act` is `request|inform|propose|query|agree|refuse|done`.
- `publish_message()` is the only place that increments `hops` or derives `requires_reply`. Loop cap: `hops > 12` blocks the publish and flags the task for human review.
- Never touch Firestore/Pub-Sub/integrations directly from a department — always through the platform client.

## A2A and Antigravity

A2A is boundary-only (exposing Sales/Support externally), never for internal CEO-to-department messaging. The Antigravity SDK is optional/non-core, scoped to one stretch feature — don't add the dependency elsewhere.

## Secrets

All third-party credentials live in Secret Manager, referenced from Firestore via `secretRef`, never the raw value in code/Firestore/committed `.env`.

Full detail and rationale: see `/docs/system_prompt.md` and `/docs/adr/`.
